This directory is intentionally kept even when empty.

The Dockerfile copies `patches/` into the image BEFORE running `npm ci`, so that
the `postinstall: patch-package` hook can see it. Docker `COPY` fails on a
missing source, so removing this file breaks the image build the moment the
directory has no other contents — which is exactly the state the repo is in
whenever there are no patches.

Keeping the directory also preserves the ordering fix itself: without it, the
`COPY patches ./patches` line has to be deleted too, and deleting it silently
restores the bug where every patch is skipped in the image while working locally
and in CI.
